 h the Korean art scene. Three artists are selected\, one per term\, across
  2027. SUPPORT: a monthly grant of KRW 1\,200\,000 (approx. USD 850\, tota
 l KRW 3\,600\,000 for the period\, adjusted to actual duration) and a priv
 ate furnished live-in studio of 46-60 square meters with access to shared 
 facilities\, galleries\, kitchen\, outdoor working zone and wireless inter
 net. Participants cover their own round-trip airfare\, meals\, local trans
 portation\, work materials and travel/medical insurance. ELIGIBILITY: open
  to artists of all nationalities except Korean citizens\, with fluency in 
 English\; previous participants of the MMCA Changdong or Goyang residencie
 s are not eligible. Applications are submitted online via mmca.go.kr only 
 (materials max 20MB). Deadline: 18 September 2026\, 18:00 KST.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: National Museum of Modern and Contemporary Art\, Korea (MMCA)\nLocat
 ion: Seoul\, South Korea (MMCA Residency Changdong)\nAward: Monthly grant 
 of KRW 1\,200\,000 (approx. USD 850)\, total KRW 3\,600\,000 for the resid
 ency period\, plus a private live-in studio (46-60 sqm) provided free of c
 harge\nDuration: Approx. 2-2.5 months\; three terms in 2027\, one artist p
 er term: 1 April - 10 June\, 1 July - 9 September\, 30 September - 9 Decem
 ber\n\nMore: https://www.mmca.go.kr/eng/pr/newsDetail.do?bdCId=20260827001
 0567&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
